<h2>1. Executive summary</h2>
<p>
  The current apex <span class="mono">camxora.com</span> is the marketing website. The music product
  currently lives at <span class="mono">music.camxora.com</span> and is served by the mature
  <span class="mono">music_web</span> application. The new Camxora templates are a complete visual and
  UX redesign of the music platform: listen-first Home, Discover, Create, Library, Charts, Community,
  artist tools, Studio, Developers, pricing, auth, and legal pages.
</p>
<p>
  The migration should not be a big-bang rewrite of the live music app. It should be a new, separately
  deployed frontend that uses the new templates, reuses the proven auth/player/streaming logic and
  existing API, and runs beside the current product until parity is proven.
</p>

<table>
  <tr><th>Decision</th><th>Recommendation</th></tr>
  <tr><td>New app</td><td><span class="mono">camxora.com/</span>, a new Next.js application on port <span class="mono">3103</span>.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Visual source</td><td>The new templates from <span class="mono">sample-1</span>. Every visible surface is rebuilt from these templates.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Logic source</td><td>Reuse <span class="mono">music_web</span> providers, player engines, auth, streaming, library, playlists, likes, and checkout. Do not copy its old UI.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Content source</td><td>Reuse <span class="mono">website/</span> legal, blog, changelog, download, and marketing content, restyled in the new templates.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Browser API</td><td>Use <span class="mono">platform_api</span> through a same-origin <span class="mono">/api/v3</span> proxy.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Provider API</td><td><span class="mono">musicapi.camxora.com</span> remains the generation provider/API product. Do not touch it.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Sandbox</td><td><span class="mono">sandbox.camxora.com</span> points to the new service. Old site remains on <span class="mono">3100</span> for rollback.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Production</td><td>Switch only <span class="mono">camxora.com</span> and <span class="mono">www</span> to <span class="mono">3103</span>. Keep <span class="mono">music.camxora.com</span> on <span class="mono">3102</span>.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Timeline</td><td>6-8 weeks for the full plan; 3-4 weeks for a limited public beta.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>2. Goals, non-goals, and assumptions</h2>

<h3>2.1 Goals</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Launch <span class="mono">camxora.com</span> as a listen-first music platform and brand home.</li>
  <li>Keep <span class="mono">music.camxora.com</span> live and unchanged during the entire build.</li>
  <li>Use the new templates for every new visible surface, with no legacy UI carried forward.</li>
  <li>Reuse existing backend behavior, accounts, credits, catalog, playback, and payments.</li>
  <li>Prove the new app on <span class="mono">sandbox.camxora.com</span> before production.</li>
  <li>Make the production switch reversible in minutes.</li>
  <li>Preserve SEO, legal pages, Khmer rendering, and mobile playback quality.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2.2 Non-goals for v1</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Rebuilding <span class="mono">musicapi</span> or its admin console.</li>
  <li>Changing the live <span class="mono">music.camxora.com</span> code, nginx, DNS, or service.</li>
  <li>Migrating user accounts or music data to a new database.</li>
  <li>Replacing the payment provider or billing engine.</li>
  <li>Cross-subdomain single sign-on across every Camxora host.</li>
  <li>Retiring the old music app on day one.</li>
  <li>Native mobile apps or changes to the desktop app binary.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2.3 Assumptions</h3>
<ul>
  <li>The new app runs on the existing sandbox and production VPS; if not, add DNS and TLS 48 hours earlier.</li>
  <li><span class="mono">platform_api</span> remains the browser-facing API and already supports auth, credits, catalog, streaming, and checkout.</li>
  <li>The current user portal at <span class="mono">app.camxora.com</span> remains available for billing and API keys during v1.</li>
  <li>The existing Font Awesome 7.3.1 local package and the original logo are approved assets.</li>
  <li>One full-time frontend engineer plus part-time design, QA, and ops is available.</li>
  <li>Production deploy happens only after an explicit approval from the owner.</li>
</ul>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<h2>3. Current state - verified from the repo</h2>

<table>
  <tr><th>Host</th><th>Current upstream</th><th>Current application</th><th>Action</th></tr>
  <tr><td class="mono">camxora.com / www</td><td class="mono">127.0.0.1:3100</td><td><span class="mono">website/</span> marketing</td><td>Leave until cutover, then switch to <span class="mono">3103</span>.</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="mono">sandbox.camxora.com</td><td class="mono">127.0.0.1:3100</td><td>sandbox website</td><td>Repoint to <span class="mono">3103</span>; keep <span class="mono">3100</span> running.</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="mono">music.camxora.com</td><td class="mono">127.0.0.1:3102</td><td><span class="mono">music_web/</span></td><td><strong>Freeze. Do not touch.</strong></td></tr>
  <tr><td class="mono">music.sandbox.camxora.com</td><td class="mono">127.0.0.1:3102</td><td>sandbox music app</td><td>Keep as old-music reference.</td></tr>
